									</P>
								</td>
		</tr><tr>
			<td class="grid_col2" align="Center">
									<P style="FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana">Title:&nbsp;
										<span id="dl_news__ctl2_Label4"><font face="Verdana" size="1">January Recruiting Awards :)</font></span></P>
									<P style="FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana">Date:
										<span id="dl_news__ctl2_Label2"><font face="Verdana" size="1">2/18/2004 1:18:59 PM</font></span></P>
									<P>
										<span id="dl_news__ctl2_Label1"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><P align=justify>Recruiting contest results - January 2004</P>
<P>The results are in, the winners are : </P>
<P>1st prize - Akashau - 35k pp&nbsp;</P>
<P>2nd prize&nbsp;- Vorkarlon - 15k pp</P>
<P>Prizes were awarded to tagged qualified members on the 15th of Feb. 2004. Good luck all with future contests and keep up the great work. </P></font></span></P>
								</td>
		</tr><tr>
			<td>
									<P>
										<HR style="WIDTH: 100%" width="100%" SIZE="3">
									</P>
								</td>
		</tr><tr>
			<td align="Center">
									<P style="FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana">Title:&nbsp;
										<span id="dl_news__ctl4_Label4"><font face="Verdana" size="1">Sol C Raid</font></span></P>
									<P style="FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana">Date:
										<span id="dl_news__ctl4_Label2"><font face="Verdana" size="1">1/11/2004 6:46:17 PM</font></span></P>
									<P>
										<span id="dl_news__ctl4_Label1"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><P>It went very well with 11 guildies. We took down a few named. Arcs was tanking. Poor Arcs. We raked in a ShadowFlame, a Obsidian Scaled Cloak, and a Planar Shield of Conflagration. Grats to the lucky bidders see you next raid. We will try to do more of these since it seems these peices&nbsp;were upgrades for some. :)</P>
<P>&nbsp;ALSO PLEASE NOTE: we have a Fear raid on the 24th to look for the chanter epic piece, and two shaman need tears, so get to working on epics :). Kael faction is still an issue for some so get to crackin :)</P></font></span></P>
								</td>
		</tr><tr>
			<td>
									<P>
										<HR style="WIDTH: 100%" width="100%" SIZE="3">
									</P>
								</td>
		</tr><tr>
			<td class="grid_col2" align="Center">
									<P style="FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana">Title:&nbsp;
										<span id="dl_news__ctl6_Label4"><font face="Verdana" size="1">Welcome our four newest members</font></span></P>
									<P style="FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana">Date:
										<span id="dl_news__ctl6_Label2"><font face="Verdana" size="1">1/10/2004 1:27:06 AM</font></span></P>
									<P>
										<span id="dl_news__ctl6_Label1"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><P>Seak, Fayloon, Vonig,&nbsp;and Tauryn have decided to join our growing Halls of Haven. Please guide them to the message boards. Seak has already updated his profile and is surfing our pages, good job. We like to read more about our members and see them accessing the calendars and such. See you in game.</P>
<P>~Akashau</P></font></span></P>
								</td>
		</tr><tr>
			<td>
									<P>
										<HR style="WIDTH: 100%" width="100%" SIZE="3">
									</P>
								</td>
		</tr><tr>
			<td align="Center">
									<P style="FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana">Title:&nbsp;
										<span id="dl_news__ctl8_Label4"><font face="Verdana" size="1">A good start</font></span></P>
									<P style="FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana">Date:
										<span id="dl_news__ctl8_Label2"><font face="Verdana" size="1">12/18/2003 11:34:18 AM</font></span></P>
									<P>
										<span id="dl_news__ctl8_Label1"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><P>Raiding seems to be back underway with relatively healthy turnout for the Chardok B raid this past Wednesday.&nbsp; Thank you to all who showed up and congratulations to Truelight on placing the winning bid for the <A Target="resource window" href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/db/item.html?item=6833">Earring of Twisted Leaves</A>.&nbsp; See everybody on Friday for a trip to the Akheva Ruins.</P></font></span></P>
								</td>
		</tr><tr>
			<td>
									<P>
										<HR style="WIDTH: 100%" width="100%" SIZE="3">
									</P>
								</td>
		</tr><tr>
			<td class="grid_col2" align="Center">
									<P style="FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana">Title:&nbsp;
										<span id="dl_news__ctl10_Label4"><font face="Verdana" size="1">PoJ Flags</font></span></P>
									<P style="FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana">Date:
										<span id="dl_news__ctl10_Label2"><font face="Verdana" size="1">11/15/2003 10:21:08 AM</font></span></P>
									<P>
										<span id="dl_news__ctl10_Label1"><font face="Verdana" size="1">Well it went very well once we got in the swing of things. Congratulations to&nbsp; Aquaella, Shimps, Bootyl, Torpedoes, Arcs, and Bewytcher on there AA, Flag, and intricate wood idol&nbsp;stat. We will try to run through again once more next month to get the few that had to leave earlier out of the way. Next month will be the last POJ trial we do as a guild event. Thanks for your support and keep up the good work :)</font></span></P>
								</td>
		</tr><tr>
			<td>
									<P>
										<HR style="WIDTH: 100%" width="100%" SIZE="3">
									</P>
								</td>
		</tr><tr>
			<td align="Center">
									<P style="FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana">Title:&nbsp;
										<span id="dl_news__ctl12_Label4"><font face="Verdana" size="1">Curzons New Shawl</font></span></P>
									<P style="FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana">Date:
										<span id="dl_news__ctl12_Label2"><font face="Verdana" size="1">11/15/2003 9:12:37 AM</font></span></P>
									<P>
										<span id="dl_news__ctl12_Label1"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><P align=justify>Congratulations Curzon on a sweater that is even better then the kind granny used to make. Wear the 8th shawl in health and prosper....the Bless Coldain Prayer Shawl is one of the hardest items on the game to get. Thank you folks that came out to help him in this quest. This quest is way harder then the epics and takes alot of dedication.&nbsp; P.S. keep up the good work on ME farms and sharding in the end you'll get a key you can be proud of ;)</P></font></span></P>
								</td>
		</tr><tr>
			<td>
									<P>
										<HR style="WIDTH: 100%" width="100%" SIZE="3">
									</P>
								</td>
		</tr><tr>
			<td class="grid_col2" align="Center">
									<P style="FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana">Title:&nbsp;
										<span id="dl_news__ctl14_Label4"><font face="Verdana" size="1">SSRA Rhag and Farm</font></span></P>
									<P style="FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana">Date:
										<span id="dl_news__ctl14_Label2"><font face="Verdana" size="1">11/10/2003 3:20:21 PM</font></span></P>
									<P>
										<span id="dl_news__ctl14_Label1"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><P align=justify>Well it went great. We got very lucky and have 3 comm2 pops&nbsp;(the <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/db/item.html?item=16281">Zeruzsh's Ring </A>ring)&nbsp;for the <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/db/quest.html?quest=1999">key to the emperors chamber</A>(the key is a very <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/danapics/ring_shissar.jpg">nice ring), </A>some items to make <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/db/quest.html?quest=1998">corrupted weapons</A>, and Rhag which dropped some nice things including the <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/db/item.html?item=13332">orb</A> for the <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/db/quest.html?quest=2000">VT key</A>.We also got two <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/db/item.html?item=16280">Zherozsh's Key</A> to the door in there that were given to the monks to pull and open for the guild both Sarsippius and Whorl have one as well as Phycos in AoP. These links should answer any question pertaining to the emperor key quest and the VT key quest. </P></font></span></P>
								</td>
		</tr><tr>
			<td>
									<P>
										<HR style="WIDTH: 100%" width="100%" SIZE="3">
									</P>
								</td>
		</tr><tr>
			<td align="Center">
									<P style="FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana">Title:&nbsp;
										<span id="dl_news__ctl16_Label4"><font face="Verdana" size="1">Epics an epidemic</font></span></P>
									<P style="FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana">Date:
										<span id="dl_news__ctl16_Label2"><font face="Verdana" size="1">11/7/2003 10:17:49 AM</font></span></P>
									<P>
										<span id="dl_news__ctl16_Label1"><font face="Verdana" size="1">Recently, we have completed alot of epics, some people have been unhappy at not having thier epics done, some have even went as far as detagging, guild jumping to us, or&nbsp; guild jumping to other guilds&nbsp;for this purpose. Epics are done and pushed by the individual...not the guild or officers. Most of the research and foot work is solo and has been done by those fortunate enough to have obtained their epics through sheer will. After the foot work, the guild then will be asked to help on main fights only. Example, farming reavers is not a guild event, shards, small drops,&nbsp;or doing research. Many of our fine members do help on these tasks but it can not be expected. These small tasks can be done with a few our your friends, guildies or not guildies. Please set goals that are realisitic for yourself and obtaining your epic :). That is what everquest is all about .....ever questing.</font></span></P>
								</td>
		</tr><tr>
			<td>
									<P>
										<HR style="WIDTH: 100%" width="100%" SIZE="3">
									</P>
								</td>
		</tr><tr>
			<td class="grid_col2" align="Center">
									<P style="FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana">Title:&nbsp;
										<span id="dl_news__ctl18_Label4"><font face="Verdana" size="1">SolC</font></span></P>
									<P style="FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana">Date:
										<span id="dl_news__ctl18_Label2"><font face="Verdana" size="1">11/6/2003 8:36:19 AM</font></span></P>
									<P>
										<span id="dl_news__ctl18_Label1"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><P align=justify>It went well last night til the end. We got a few nice pieces including the hard piece for <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/db/item.html?item=22782">Ghaib's Flame-Forged Longsword</A>. Hopefully someone will take interest in this worhtwhile quest in the guild, I beleive the Crystallized Soul of Fire can be MQ'd. Friday is the Deep Farm for Shards. It's a harder to reach shard so please be present :).</P></font></span></P>
								</td>
		</tr><tr>
			<td>
									<P>
										<HR style="WIDTH: 100%" width="100%" SIZE="3">
									</P>
								</td>
		</tr><tr>
			<td align="Center">
									<P style="FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana">Title:&nbsp;
										<span id="dl_news__ctl20_Label4"><font face="Verdana" size="1">HoT - Get that Faction :)</font></span></P>
									<P style="FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana">Date:
										<span id="dl_news__ctl20_Label2"><font face="Verdana" size="1">10/30/2003 8:09:04 AM</font></span></P>
									<P>
										<span id="dl_news__ctl20_Label1"><font face="Verdana" size="1">Last night was a HUGE success. I can not stress enough on faction for CoV. Please if your still KOS get to Kael. We had some ultra hard to get drops last night including the Unadorned Leather Tunic and Unadorned Chain Tunic. Grats to lucky winners :). No deaths keep up the fantastic work.</font></span></P>
								</td>
		</tr><tr>
			<td>
									<P>
										<HR style="WIDTH: 100%" width="100%" SIZE="3">
									</P>
								</td>
		</tr><tr>
			<td class="grid_col2" align="Center">
									<P style="FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana">Title:&nbsp;
										<span id="dl_news__ctl22_Label4"><font face="Verdana" size="1">Fear - Whos who....grats True ;)</font></span></P>
									<P style="FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana">Date:
										<span id="dl_news__ctl22_Label2"><font face="Verdana" size="1">10/26/2003 8:07:38 AM</font></span></P>
									<P>
										<span id="dl_news__ctl22_Label1"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><P align=left><FONT size=4>Truelight got the last piece of his Wizard epic. WOOT. Good work all and thank you for your patience. </FONT>Also a special thanks&nbsp;to&nbsp;Menelaeus (MA), Qmanorus (ubbah Mage), Clerark (great healer), Bluudson, Horator,&nbsp;Linlail (who waited all day), and Aquaella (she was at raid time waiting noon&nbsp;and late after the kill at 11 looking to help). Some participants got partial credit for the raid for waiting and were added to the raid effort. This was an odd one, We waited over 8 hours for all the members we needed to log on ;)</P></font></span></P>
								</td>
		</tr><tr>
			<td>
									<P>
										<HR style="WIDTH: 100%" width="100%" SIZE="3">
									</P>
								</td>
		</tr><tr>
			<td align="Center">
									<P style="FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana">Title:&nbsp;
										<span id="dl_news__ctl24_Label4"><font face="Verdana" size="1">HoT</font></span></P>
									<P style="FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana">Date:
										<span id="dl_news__ctl24_Label2"><font face="Verdana" size="1">10/23/2003 9:41:59 AM</font></span></P>
									<P>
										<span id="dl_news__ctl24_Label1"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><P>Good work&nbsp;especially being shy some key classes. We got 2 plate drops for the <A href=http://everquest.allakhazam.com/qgen/Skyshrine.html Target="resource window">Skyshrine Quest</A>. One was won by Bennan and one by Darsus. </P>
<P>Please be aware if you don't come to raids very often most likely you will not have the points needed to bid. Sometimes all you need is 1 point to win and you get 3-4 points per raid, so don't be discouraged they add up fast. See you in game.</P></font></span></P>
								</td>
		</tr><tr>
			<td>
									<P>
										<HR style="WIDTH: 100%" width="100%" SIZE="3">
									</P>
								</td>
		</tr><tr>
			<td class="grid_col2" align="Center">
									<P style="FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana">Title:&nbsp;
										<span id="dl_news__ctl26_Label4"><font face="Verdana" size="1">Sleepers Key</font></span></P>
									<P style="FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana">Date:
										<span id="dl_news__ctl26_Label2"><font face="Verdana" size="1">10/19/2003 10:52:16 PM</font></span></P>
									<P>
										<span id="dl_news__ctl26_Label1"><font face="Verdana" size="1">Grats Ghruk on the Shard of Hsagra's Talisman for the <A href=http://everquest.allakhazam.com/db/quest.html?quest=938 Target="resource window">Sleeper's Tomb Key</A>. This appears to be a single person key we will all need this type of item :) off some dragon somewhere or something please read up on it if your curious</font></span></P>
								</td>
		</tr><tr>
			<td>
									<P>
										<HR style="WIDTH: 100%" width="100%" SIZE="3">
									</P>
								</td>
		</tr><tr>
			<td align="Center">
									<P style="FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana">Title:&nbsp;
										<span id="dl_news__ctl28_Label4"><font face="Verdana" size="1">Last night's Deep Raid - AKA Farm</font></span></P>
									<P style="FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana">Date:
										<span id="dl_news__ctl28_Label2"><font face="Verdana" size="1">10/18/2003 9:33:05 AM</font></span></P>
									<P>
										<span id="dl_news__ctl28_Label1"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><P align=center><STRONG><FONT face=Tahoma color=#d3d3d3>Congratulations Deveau on getting all 10 shards completed.</FONT></STRONG></P>
<P align=justify>Last night was very successful. We got 7 shards, we needed 5 more but sharding is time consuming. This is all for the VT key. The sharding is the time consuming part, as well as the com1 and com2 piece. I encourage you when your bored to work together on the coms and the ME shard (they are the worst). After raid last night we went down to SSRA and farmed 4 shards there as well.&nbsp; We also farmed two of the bags that are needed to combine the <A href=http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/danapics/ring_shissar.jpg target="resource window">Emp Ring</A>. Good luck to us all. This is a long quest it will probably take 4 months to complete with helping each other. It is the hardest key in the game....and such a great feeling when you know your the owner of the pieces or the full key....we will need a few more key classes and members before we can kill the emp of SSRA. The parts combines in the <A href=http://everquest.allakhazam.com/db/recipe.html?recipe=4217 target="resource window">bag are listed here</A>. Once we get into the emp we need to kill him with <A href=http://everquest.allakhazam.com/db/quest.html?quest=1998 target="resource window">special weapons.</A>&nbsp;The emp drops whats known as the rift. This combines with the shards to form the VT key. Next week the FG Farm on&nbsp; Friday. We already farmed a few of these. If you see us working on sharding and do not possess that shard or just want to help &gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;LET US KNOW :)&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;</P></font></span></P>
								</td>
		</tr><tr>
			<td>
									<P>
										<HR style="WIDTH: 100%" width="100%" SIZE="3">
									</P>
								</td>
		</tr><tr>
			<td class="grid_col2" align="Center">
									<P style="FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana">Title:&nbsp;
										<span id="dl_news__ctl30_Label4"><font face="Verdana" size="1">Chard B Raid - Follow up</font></span></P>
									<P style="FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana">Date:
										<span id="dl_news__ctl30_Label2"><font face="Verdana" size="1">10/16/2003 9:23:14 AM</font></span></P>
									<P>
										<span id="dl_news__ctl30_Label1"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><P align=justify><SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: 'Times New Roman'; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-ansi-language: EN-US; mso-fareast-language: EN-US; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA"><FONT face=Verdana size=2>This was essentially a farm for the </FONT><A target="resource window" href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/fpics/black_enchanted_amulet.jpg"><FONT face=Verdana size=2>Black Enchanted Amulet</FONT></A><FONT face=Verdana size=2>. This item has some nice stats and resists. We also began working on collecting more pages for the </FONT><A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/fpics/golem_heart_ring.jpg" target="resource window"><FONT face=Verdana size=2>Golem Heart Ring</FONT></A><FONT face=Verdana size=2>. There are 4 gems and 4 pages. The halls are a good place to collect these items. We have a few bags completed for the combine of the gems (the gems are not MQable). The bag is droppable for the combines; there is no need to collect the staffs of suffering unless you want your own bag. When you get 4 of either (or we do as a guild on the pages) we will run back down and do the turn-ins with you. It is rumored this zone is temporary, so if you want something from it you might want to get crackin ;)</FONT></SPAN></P></font></span></P>
								</td>
		</tr><tr>
			<td>
									<P>
										<HR style="WIDTH: 100%" width="100%" SIZE="3">
									</P>
								</td>
		</tr><tr>
			<td align="Center">
									<P style="FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana">Title:&nbsp;
										<span id="dl_news__ctl32_Label4"><font face="Verdana" size="1">Dragonecropolis </font></span></P>
									<P style="FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana">Date:
										<span id="dl_news__ctl32_Label2"><font face="Verdana" size="1">10/12/2003 8:50:31 PM</font></span></P>
									<P>
										<span id="dl_news__ctl32_Label1"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><P>Well the raid went very well with 17 folks showing up to play. We didn't get our dragon but we got a few ok pieces and one very nice piece, grats Bennan.</P>
<P>We implemented our point system tonight and have nearly moved all the boards here. Please be sure to sign into the new webboard. Hopefully this will be the last home of HoH Guild status :)</P>
<P>On your right is the quick links. The new looting rules (not in stone) are posted on page two of it. On your left is a section marked Player Roster. There is where you can find your points available. Tonights purchases and credit/debits were entered. I really appreciate your patience during this transition. The point system will enable us to not only distribute loot evenly (and still nbg basis) but it will allow us to wrap up the raids faster. The no drop loot will be distrubuted at the raid, the non-nodrop will be after the raid in the POK port in. See you all in game :). If you have any questions please feel free to ask me or anyone that has a clue :)</P></font></span></P>
								</td>
		</tr><tr>
			<td>
									<P>
										<HR style="WIDTH: 100%" width="100%" SIZE="3">
									</P>
								</td>
		</tr><tr>
			<td class="grid_col2" align="Center">
									<P style="FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana">Title:&nbsp;
										<span id="dl_news__ctl34_Label4"><font face="Verdana" size="1">PoN - Maze</font></span></P>
									<P style="FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana">Date:
										<span id="dl_news__ctl34_Label2"><font face="Verdana" size="1">10/8/2003 11:36:13 PM</font></span></P>
									<P>
										<span id="dl_news__ctl34_Label1"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><P align=justify>Tonight was very successful. Poor Junaper had a run of bad luck, it appears where ever she stood was the lucky spawn point of the mobs 90% of the time, the other 10% they just ran straight to her :(. We got our first group of 16 flagged. 14 members of the raid force were HoH, Raadian tanked. Great tanking :). The chanters were mezzing like the wind and saving all our butts. The main guy hit for about 1100plus....that will definately leave a mark. He had a ton of HP but he was slowed right off (thanks to &nbsp;Ghruk I believe) or we might (would have wiped). This was about the only battle that Junaper lived through and we were happy to not have to dust her poor body off. Her sacrafices bought time for mezzes though :). Hazzaaaah! Poor Deveau took two death as well....</P>
<P align=justify>Sadly, this didn't make the totem stronger but does grant the first 16 access to PoNB. I would like to thank Linlail and Cukkin for attending as well. Grats to all the lucky flagged ;). It was big &nbsp;fun. </P></font></span></P>
								</td>
		</tr><tr>
			<td>
									<P>
										<HR style="WIDTH: 100%" width="100%" SIZE="3">
									</P>
								</td>
		</tr><tr>
			<td align="Center">
									<P style="FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana">Title:&nbsp;
										<span id="dl_news__ctl36_Label4"><font face="Verdana" size="1">Cazic Thul is down....</font></span></P>
									<P style="FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana">Date:
										<span id="dl_news__ctl36_Label2"><font face="Verdana" size="1">9/11/2003 2:05:24 AM</font></span></P>
									<P>
										<span id="dl_news__ctl36_Label1"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><P align=justify>Tonight was exciting.&nbsp; We broke in Fear with 13. We cleared the PoF with less then 20 people in 3 hours. The first try at Ct was with 20 members, we wiped. The second try was with 29. Thank you members of other guilds for the use of your extra melee and clerics. Thank you AoP for standing beside us as usual</P></font></span></P>
								</td>
		</tr>
	</table>
						
</td></tr></table>
